# Exact matrix certificates for two O'Nan local inverters

Twelve balanced products in the literal 45-dimensional GF(7) representation
verify two words in the ATLAS max5 generators. The first inverts the marked
central cubic and fixes the A₄ three-cycle; the second inverts that three-cycle.
The scalar four disappears only after the explicit projective projection.

The inputs are the checked word matrices from `E9A4.WordMatrices`. Packed
base-seven rows and the proved Horner checker certify ordinary matrix products.
Word discovery is not a proof assumption. The source application is
Aschbacher–Smith A.2.19, printed p.41.
